# Everything the image must never receive.
#
# Two jobs. First, keep the build context small and the layer cache stable —
# without this, `COPY src/ src/` also ships target/ and .git, and every commit
# invalidates every cached layer. Second, and more important: keep secrets and
# host state out of the image. Anything copied in is permanently readable in
# the layer history even if a later step deletes it.

# --- Secrets and local-only configuration --------------------------------
# .env holds the real Resend key on a developer machine; the *-local and
# *-secret property files are where developer credentials live by convention
# (see .gitignore). None of them may ever enter an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
application-local.properties
application-local.yml
application-secret.properties
application-secret.yml

# --- Build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# The image builds its own jar. Copying a host-built target/ in would let a
# stale local artifact silently become the deployed one.
target/

# --- Runtime state --------------------------------------------------------
# User-uploaded files live in a volume, never baked into the image.
uploads/

# --- Version control and tooling -----------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.idea
.vscode
.run
.claude
.cursor
*.iml

# --- Docs, CI and compose (not needed to compile) -------------------------
docs/
*.md
!README.md
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# --- OS noise -------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
